-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/state.json" "file_sha256" "c74fda06dd1c9a039fcb37be34cac21e575f1f99f41ad1f4f644ada66e6b2ca3"} {"question" "q-75506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}0x-y+z=1 \\\\ x+y+2z=-1 \\\\ x+3y-z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=0,\\,b=2,\\,c=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/state.json" "file_sha256" "c74fda06dd1c9a039fcb37be34cac21e575f1f99f41ad1f4f644ada66e6b2ca3"} {"question" "q-75506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4877b59e1a51f5e28beeeccc2b222edc8519c5e2bce559efbb9c245a1e9da451"} {"question" "q-75506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/