stem in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2,\\,b=0,\\,c=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/state.json" "file_sha256" "c74fda06dd1c9a039fcb37be34cac21e575f1f99f41ad1f4f644ada66e6b2ca3"} {"question" "q-75509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4877b59e1a51f5e28beeeccc2b222edc8519c5e2bce559efbb9c245a1e9da451"} {"question" "q-75509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/state.json" "file_sha256" "c74fda06dd1c9a039fcb37be34cac21e575f1f99f41ad1f4f644ada66e6b2ca3"} {"question" "q-75509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a=-5,\\,b=-3,\\,c=-3"] ["math" "a=-5,\\,b=0,\\,c=-3"] ["math" "a=2,\\,b=-3,\\,c=-1"] ["math" "a=2,\\,b=0,\\,c=-1"] ["math" "a=2,\\,b=1,\\,c=-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/state.json" "file_sha256" "c74fda06dd1c9a039fcb37be34cac21e575f1f99f41ad1f4f644ada66e6b2ca3"} {"question" "q-75509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a=2,\\,b=0,\\,c=-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/state.json" "file_sha256" "c74fda06dd1c9a039fcb37be34cac21e575f1f99f41ad1f4f644ada66e6b2ca3"} {"question" "q-9720" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y+2z-x=1 \\\\ 6y+3x-2z=2 \\\\ x+3z-y=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & b & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/state.json" "file_sha256" "c74fda06dd1c9a039fcb37be34cac21e575f1f99f41ad1f4f644ada66e6b2ca3"} {"question" "q-9720" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-x+y+2z=1 \\\\ 3x+6y-2z=2 \\\\ x-y+3z=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-1,\\,b=6,\\,c=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/state.json" "file_sha256" "c74fda06dd1c9a039fcb37be34cac21e575f1f99f41ad1f4f644ada66e6b2ca3"} {"question" "q-9720" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4877b59e1a51f5e28beeeccc2b222edc8519c5e2bce559efbb9c245a1e9da451"} {"question" "q-9720" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/state.json" "file_sha256" "c74fda06dd1c9a039fcb37be34cac21e575f1f99f41ad1f4f644ada66e6b2ca3"} {"question" "q-9720" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a=-1,\\,b=6,\\,c=-3"] ["math" "a=-1,\\,b=6,\\,c=3"] ["math" "a=1,\\,b=2,\\,c=-3"] ["math" "a=1,\\,b=6,\\,c=2"] ["math" "a=3,\\,b=-1,\\,c=-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/state.json" "file_sha256" "c74fda06dd1c9a039fcb37be34cac21e575f1f99f41ad1f4f644ada66e6b2ca3"} {"question" "q-9720" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a=-1,\\,b=6,\\,c=-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/state.json" "file_sha256" "c74fda06dd1c9a039fcb37be34cac21e575f1f99f41ad1f4f644ada66e6b2ca3"} {"question" "q-75500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-2y+3z=7 \\\\ x+z=-1 \\\\ 3z-2x+y=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & b & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/state.json" "file_sha256" "c74fda06dd1c9a039fcb37be34cac21e575f1f99f41ad1f4f644ada66e6b2ca3"} {"question" "q-75500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}0x-2y+3z=7 \\\\ x+0y+z=-1 \\\\ -2x+y+3z=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=0,\\,b=0,\\,c=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/state.json" "file_sha256" "c74fda06dd1c9a039fcb37be34cac21e575f1f99f41ad1f4f644ada66e6b2ca3"} {"question" "q-75500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4877b59e1a51f5e28beeeccc2b222edc8519c5e2bce559efbb9c245a1e9da451"} {"question" "q-75500" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/