\begin{aligned}a & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & b & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/example-4518.json" "file_sha256" "18e68fafb8b2de1af96577a6bcd8efa08b752c29b391e9577282a7f36f5c1aba"} {"question" "e-4518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+0z=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/example-4518.json" "file_sha256" "18e68fafb8b2de1af96577a6bcd8efa08b752c29b391e9577282a7f36f5c1aba"} {"question" "e-4519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ z-x+2=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & a & 1 \\\\ b & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/example-4519.json" "file_sha256" "00a9c6203c8116ac89df8de2ccc1d12b50bb067c9df5d3e5f10ca42b2535a35f"} {"question" "e-4519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995396/example-4519.json" "file_sha256" "00a9c6203c8116ac89df8de2ccc1d12b50bb067c9df5d3e5f10ca42b2535a35f"}] "usage" {"e-4519" [] "e-4518" []} "basis" 1060 "retractions" [[17592186059490 :question/problem "The system of equations\n${6x + 4y = 1; x - 8y - z =-2; 3x + 2y - 2z = 1$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}a & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & b & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWhat are the values of $a$, $b$ and $c$?"] [17592186059490 :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{6x + 4y + 0z = 1; x - 8y - z =-2; 3x + 2y - 2z = 1\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nbecomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=6$, $b=2$, and $c=-2$."] [17592186059491 :question/problem "The system of equations\n${2x - y + z = 4; z - x + 2 =-1; 2y - 2x - 4z =-4$\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & a & 1 \\\\ b & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$\nWhat are the values of $a$, $b$ and $c$?"] [17592186059491 :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{2x - y + z = 4; - x + 0y + z =-3; - 2x + 2y - 4z =-4\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation\n\n$$\nA\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nbecomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore $a=0$, $b=-2$, $c=-3$."]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
